<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shaka (Zulu king)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shaka was the king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> who built the Zulu kingdom into a powerful military state in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> from the 1810s. His wars and state-building are associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a>, a period of upheaval and migration across southern Africa. Groups displaced in the Mfecane invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a> and destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> state.</p></div>
